      "writtenOn": "2022-10-03T21:24:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Regarding BatterySet: yes, I think this is much better. however, I avoided doing something like this because during the API design phase you indicated nested structs were problematic for DBus; is that no longer true?\n\nI disagree somewhat regarding prioritization. Specifically this case:\n\n1. A device exists which supplies battery information from multiple sources (A and B).\n2. Sometimes when the device connects BatteryProviderManager receives information from A first, so the user sees information displayed according to what A says.\n3. User reboots their machine, disconnects device, etc. and in this instance information from B is received first instead.\n\nIf A and B do not send information in the same format, the user may get very difference experiences. Example: A represents battery information as an average of all batteries while B breaks out a Battery for each battery. If we have a deterministic way of determining what should be shown then we\u0027ll be consistent, regardless of which is actually the better source.",
      "parentUuid": "f731b03e_0e03fa4a",
      "revId": "69d7b7b84f391cb92867abfc4dd20ebb9741759d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9635b972_5ff2cba7",
